-- title:
--   Unipotent inertia at the auxiliary prime over T_Q
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional $k$-linear representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ that is trivial on the absolute Galois group of some number field and is absolutely irreducible (its base change to $\overline k$ has no invariant subspace other than $0$ and the whole space). Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N\ge 1$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\nmid N$, $r\ne p$ and $p\nmid r-1$, such that $\bar\rho$ is unramified at $r$ (for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $r$ a non-unit of $P$, every element of the inertia subgroup at $P$ acts trivially) and such that $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\ne (r+1)^2$ for every $P$ lying over $r$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius element at $r$ for $P$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$ prime, $q\notin S$ — to $k$, such that for all primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ and all Frobenius elements $\sigma$ at $\ell$ one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, let $\pi_i:(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ be group homomorphisms (multiplicatively written target), and let $\alpha:\mathrm{Fin}\,t\to k$. Assume the Hecke operators at level $L=N(\prod_i q_i)r$ with the subgroup $H_Q$ commute pairwise (`OpComm`) and commute with the diamond operators (`DiaComm`), and let $\mathbb T=\mathrm{HeckeRing}$ be the resulting $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of endomorphisms of the localised cohomology module, assumed local, Noetherian, $\mathfrak m_{\mathbb T}$-adically complete, module-finite over $\mathcal O$, with $\mathcal O\to\mathbb T$ a local homomorphism inducing a surjection $\mathcal O\to\mathbb T/\mathfrak m_{\mathbb T}$. Let $\rho'$ be a representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on a free $\mathbb T$-module of rank two, continuous in the $\mathfrak m_{\mathbb T}$-adic sense, such that $\operatorname{tr}\rho'(\sigma)=T_\ell$ for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$, and such that the residual representation of $\rho'$ is isomorphic to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Then $\rho'$ is unipotent on inertia at $r$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $r$ as a non-unit and every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup at $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho'(\sigma)$ equals $(X-1)^2$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility statement at the auxiliary prime $r$ for the Galois representation carried by the Taylor–Wiles Hecke ring $\mathbb T_Q$: the inertia at $r$ acts unipotently, which is the shape imposed by the deformation condition at $r$. It is the companion, at $q=r$, of the corresponding statement at primes dividing $N$, and it is used to prove that $\rho'$ is in fact unramified at $r$ under the hypotheses $p\nmid r-1$ and $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\ne(r+1)^2$.
